 The gate and the effect row in TypeEnv are one change and must stay
 one change. A builtin that is gated here but typed pure there is
 worse than an ungated one: the caller never declares Network, so the
 manifest never grants the bit, so the call is denied and hands back
 -1 with nothing to say why. That has cost this project three
 debugging sessions (process-kill, device-seed, the identity readers).
 The row is what earns the bit; the gate is what spends it.

